---
title: "claimTokenAllocation (LegionPreLiquidOpenApplicationSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_investor: caller is investor
    q_check_investor --> q_check_settled: hasSettled == false
    q_check_investor --> q_revert_settled: already settled
    q_revert_settled --> [*]: revert AlreadySettled
    q_check_settled --> q_check_supplied: tokensSupplied == true AND saleResultsPublished
    q_check_settled --> q_revert_precond: preconditions not met
    q_revert_precond --> [*]: revert PreconditionsNotMet
    q_check_supplied --> q_verify_merkle: verify claim Merkle proof (allocation + vesting terms)
    q_check_supplied --> q_revert_proof: invalid Merkle proof
    q_revert_proof --> [*]: revert InvalidMerkleProof
    q_verify_merkle --> q_check_vesting: proof valid, allocation verified
    q_check_vesting --> q_deploy_vesting: vesting terms present
    q_check_vesting --> q_direct_transfer: no vesting (immediate)
    q_deploy_vesting --> q_transfer_vested: deploy vesting contract
    q_transfer_vested --> q_settle: transfer tokens to vesting contract
    q_direct_transfer --> q_settle: transfer tokens directly to investor
    q_settle --> [*]: hasSettled = true, emit TokensClaimed

    note right of q_verify_merkle
        INV-001: Merkle proof verification (vs dual signature in Approved variant)
        INV-002: allocation amount set by project evaluation, not SAFT
        INV-003: vesting contract deployed per-investor if vesting terms present
        INV-004: post-capital-withdrawal vesting modifications prohibited
    end note
